positive_text:
Determine all integers $n \ge 3$ for which it is possible to assign real numbers to each vertex of a regular $n$-gon such that the following two conditions are satisfied:
(1) For any three vertices $a, b, c$ in clockwise order, the value at $a$ is equal to the absolute difference of the values at $b$ and $c$;
(2) The total sum of all the values assigned to the vertices is 1.

negatives.text:
Find all integers $n \ge 3$ such that one can write a number (not necessarily an integer) into each vertex of a regular $n$-gon in such a way that both following conditions are met:
(1) Whenever three consecutive vertices of the $n$-gon, taken clockwise, contain numbers $x, y$ and $z$, respectively, the equality $x = y + z$ holds;
(2) The sum of the numbers in all vertices of the $n$-gon is 1.

Find all integers $n \ge 3$ such that one can write a number (not necessarily an integer) into each vertex of a regular $n$-gon in such a way that both following conditions are met:
(1) Whenever three consecutive vertices of the $n$-gon, taken clockwise, contain numbers $x, y$ and $z$, respectively, the equality $x = |y + z|$ holds;
(2) The sum of the numbers in all vertices of the $n$-gon is 1.

Find all integers $n \ge 3$ such that one can write a number (not necessarily an integer) into each vertex of a regular $n$-gon in such a way that both following conditions are met:
(1) Whenever three consecutive vertices of the $n$-gon, taken clockwise, contain numbers $x, y$ and $z$, respectively, the equality $x = |y - z|$ holds;
(2) The product of the numbers in all vertices of the $n$-gon is 1.

positive_text:
Find all non-decreasing sequences $\left(a_{1}, a_{2}, \ldots, a_{2020}\right)$ of non-negative real numbers such that:
(i) $a_{2020} \leq a_{1}+1$;
(ii) there is a rearrangement $\left(b_{1}, b_{2}, \ldots, b_{2020}\right)$ of $\left(a_{1}, a_{2}, \ldots, a_{2020}\right)$ satisfying
$$
\sum_{i=1}^{2020}\left(\left(a_{i}+1\right)\left(b_{i}+1\right)\right)^{2} = 8 \sum_{i=1}^{2020} a_{i}^{3}
$$

negatives.text:
Find all lists $\left(x_{1}, x_{2}, \ldots, x_{2020}\right)$ of non-negative real numbers such that the following three conditions are all satisfied:
(i) $x_{1} \leq x_{2} \leq \ldots \leq x_{2020}$;
(ii) $x_{2020} \leq x_{1}+1$;
(iii) there is a permutation $\left(y_{1}, y_{2}, \ldots, y_{2020}\right)$ of $\left(x_{1}, x_{2}, \ldots, x_{2020}\right)$ such that
$$
\sum_{i=1}^{2020}\left(\left(x_{i}+1\right)\left(y_{i}+1\right)\right)^{2} = 9 \sum_{i=1}^{2020} x_{i}^{3}
$$

Find all lists $\left(x_{1}, x_{2}, \ldots, x_{2020}\right)$ of non-negative real numbers such that the following three conditions are all satisfied:
(i) $x_{1} \leq x_{2} \leq \ldots \leq x_{2020}$;
(ii) $x_{2020} \leq x_{1}+1$;
(iii) there is a permutation $\left(y_{1}, y_{2}, \ldots, y_{2020}\right)$ of $\left(x_{1}, x_{2}, \ldots, x_{2020}\right)$ such that
$$
\sum_{i=1}^{2020}\left(\left(x_{i}+1\right)\left(y_{i}+1\right)\right)^{2} = 8 \sum_{i=1}^{2020} x_{i}^{2}
$$

positive_text:
Soit $ABC$ un triangle. Soient $D \in [AC]$ et $E \in [AB]$ tels que $CD = BE$. Soit $P$ le point d'intersection de $(BD)$ et $(CE)$. Soient $K$ et $L$ les milieux respectifs de $[BE]$ et $[CD]$. Soit $Q$ l'autre point d'intersection des cercles circonscrits à $BEP$ et $CDP$. Soit $R$ le point d'intersection des perpendiculaires respectives à $(QK)$ et $(QL)$ passant par $K$ et $L$. Démontrer que
1) $R$ est situé sur le cercle circonscrit de $ABC$;
2) $Q$ est sur la bissectrice de l'angle $\widehat{BAC}$.

Déterminer tous les quadruplets $ (a, b, c, m) $ d'entiers strictement positifs tels que :\begin{itemize}
\item $a$ et $b$ sont des nombres premiers,
\item $a+b$ n’est pas divisible par $3$,
\item $a + b = c (a - b)^m$.
\end{itemize}

negatives.text:
Trouver tous les quadruplets $ (p, q, r, n) $ d’entiers strictement positifs vérifiant :\begin{itemize}
\item $p$ et $q$ sont premiers,
\item $p+q$ n’est pas divisible par $3$,
\item $p + q = r (p + q)^n$.
\end{itemize}

Trouver tous les quadruplets $ (p, q, r, n) $ d’entiers strictement positifs vérifiant :\begin{itemize}
\item $p$ et $q$ sont premiers,
\item $p+q$ n’est pas divisible par $3$,
\item $p - q = r (p + q)^n$.
\end{itemize}

positive_text:
Déterminer toutes les valeurs possibles pour $f(2018)$ où $f$ est une fonction de $\mathbb{Q}$ dans $\mathbb{R}_{+}$ vérifiant les trois propriétés suivantes:
- $f(2) = 0.5$;
- pour tout rationnel $x$, $f(x) \leq 1$ implique $f(x+1) \leq 1$;
- $f(xy) = f(x) \cdot f(y)$ pour tous rationnels $x$ et $y$.

negatives.text:
Trouver toutes les valeurs possibles pour $f(2018)$ où $f$ est une fonction de $\mathbb{Q}$ dans $\mathbb{R}_{+}$ vérifiant les trois conditions suivantes:
- $f(2) = 2$;
- pour tout rationnel $x$, si $f(x) \leq 1$, alors $f(x+1) \leq 1$;
- $f(x+y) = f(x) + f(y)$ pour tous rationnels $x$ et $y$.

Trouver toutes les valeurs possibles pour $f(2018)$ où $f$ est une fonction de $\mathbb{Q}$ dans $\mathbb{R}_{+}$ vérifiant les trois conditions suivantes:
- $f(2) = 1/2$;
- pour tout rationnel $x$, si $f(x) < 1$, alors $f(x+1) < 1$;
- $f(xy) = f(x) f(y)$ pour tous rationnels $x$ et $y$.

positive_text:
Déterminer toutes les fonctions $f: \mathbb{N}_{\geqslant 1} \to \mathbb{N}_{\geqslant 0}$ satisfaisant les deux propriétés suivantes : 
1. $f(xy) = f(x) + f(y)$ pour tous $x, y \in \mathbb{N}_{\geqslant 1}$;
2. il existe une infinité d'entiers $n \in \mathbb{N}_{\geqslant 1}$ tels que $f(k) = f(n - k)$ pour tout $k$ vérifiant $1 \leqslant k \leqslant n - 1$.

negatives.text:
Trouver les fonctions $f: \mathbb{N}_{\geqslant 1} \mapsto \mathbb{N}_{\geqslant 0}$ vérifiant les deux conditions suivantes : 
1. $f(x y)=f(x) + f(y) + 1$ pour tous les entiers $x \geqslant 1$ et $y \geqslant 1$;
2. il existe une infinité d'entiers $n \geqslant 1$ tels que l'égalité $f(k)=f(n-k)$ est vraie pour tout entier $k$ tel que $1 \leqslant k \leqslant n-1$.

Trouver les fonctions $f: \mathbb{N}_{\geqslant 1} \mapsto \mathbb{N}_{\geqslant 0}$ vérifiant les deux conditions suivantes : 
1. $f(x + y)=f(x) + f(y)$ pour tous les entiers $x \geqslant 1$ et $y \geqslant 1$;
2. il existe une infinité d'entiers $n \geqslant 1$ tels que l'égalité $f(k)=f(n - k)$ est vraie pour tout entier $k$ tel que $1 \leqslant k \leqslant n-1$.

positive_text:
Determine all positive integers $n$ such that there exist $n$ real numbers $a_1, a_2, \dots, a_n$ in the interval $[-4, 2]$ satisfying the following:
- $\sum_{i=1}^n a_i \ge n$;
- $\sum_{i=1}^n a_i^2 \le 4n$;
- $\sum_{i=1}^n a_i^4 \ge 34n$.

negatives.text:
Determine all integers $n \ge 1$ for which there exist $n$ real numbers $x_1, x_2, \dots, x_n$ in the interval $[-4, 2]$ such that:
- the sum of these real numbers is at most $n$;
- the sum of their squares is at most $4n$;
- the sum of their fourth powers is at least $34n$.

Determine all integers $n \ge 1$ for which there exist $n$ real numbers $x_1, x_2, \dots, x_n$ in the interval $[-4, 2]$ such that:
- the sum of these real numbers is at least $n$;
- the sum of their cubes is at most $4n$;
- the sum of their fourth powers is at least $34n$.

Determine all integers $n \ge 1$ for which there exist $n$ real numbers $x_1, x_2, \dots, x_n$ in the interval $[-3, 2]$ such that:
- the sum of these real numbers is at least $n$;
- the sum of their squares is at most $4n$;
- the sum of their fourth powers is at least $34n$.

positive_text:
Let $\tau(n)$ be the number of positive divisors of $n$. Determine all functions $f: \mathbb{N} \rightarrow \mathbb{N}$ satisfying the following:
(i) $\tau(f(x)) = x$ for all $x \in \mathbb{N}$;
(ii) $f(x y)$ divides $(x - 1) y^{x y - 1} f(x)$ for all $x, y \in \mathbb{N}$.

negatives.text:
Let $\tau(n)$ be the number of positive divisors of $n$. Determine all functions $f: \mathbb{N} \rightarrow \mathbb{N}$ satisfying the following:
(i) $\tau(f(x)) = x$ for all $x \in \mathbb{N}$;
(ii) $f(x y)$ divides $(x + 1) y^{x y - 1} f(x)$ for all $x, y \in \mathbb{N}$.

Let $\tau(n)$ be the number of positive divisors of $n$. Determine all functions $f: \mathbb{N} \rightarrow \mathbb{N}$ satisfying the following:
(i) $\tau(f(x)) = x$ for all $x \in \mathbb{N}$;
(ii) $f(x y)$ divides $(x - 1) y^{x y} f(x)$ for all $x, y \in \mathbb{N}$.

Let $\tau(n)$ be the number of positive divisors of $n$. Determine all functions $f: \mathbb{N} \rightarrow \mathbb{N}$ satisfying the following:
(i) $\tau(f(x)) = x$ for all $x \in \mathbb{N}$;
(ii) $f(x y)$ divides $(x - 1)^2 y^{x y - 1} f(x)$ for all $x, y \in \mathbb{N}$.

positive_text:
Let $R$ be the circumradius of triangle $ABC$, with side lengths $a = BC$, $b = CA$, $c = AB$, and exradii $r_a, r_b, r_c$ opposite $A, B, C$, respectively. If $2R \leq r_a$, prove that
(i) $a$ is the largest side of the triangle;
(ii) $2R > r_b$ and $2R > r_c$.

Let $a_{1}$ be a given positive integer. A sequence $\langle a_{n}\rangle_{n=1}^{\infty} = \langle a_{1}, a_{2}, a_{3}, \cdots \rangle$ of positive integers is defined such that $a_{n}$, for $n \geq 2$, is formed by adding a nonzero digit of $a_{n-1}$ to $a_{n-1}$. Prove that
(a) the sequence contains an even number;
(b) the sequence contains infinitely many even numbers.

negatives.text:
Let $x_{1}$ be a given positive integer. A sequence $\langle x_{n}\rangle_{n=1}^{\infty} = \langle x_{1}, x_{2}, x_{3}, \cdots \rangle$ of positive integers is such that $x_{n}$, for $n \geq 2$, is obtained from $x_{n-1}$ by subtracting some nonzero digit of $x_{n-1}$. Prove that
(a) the sequence has an even number;
(b) the sequence has infinitely many even numbers.

Let $x_{1}$ be a given positive integer. A sequence $\langle x_{n}\rangle_{n=1}^{\infty} = \langle x_{1}, x_{2}, x_{3}, \cdots \rangle$ of positive integers is such that $x_{n}$, for $n \geq 2$, is obtained from $x_{n-1}$ by multiplying $x_{n-1}$ by some nonzero digit of $x_{n-1}$. Prove that
(a) the sequence has an even number;
(b) the sequence has infinitely many even numbers.

