positive_text:
Two circles $C_1$ and $C_2$, with centres at $D$ and $E$ respectively, touch at $B$. The circle with diameter $DE$ intersects $C_1$ at $H$ and $C_2$ at $K$, both on the same side of the line $DE$. Extending $HK$ meets $C_1$ again at $L$ and $C_2$ again at $M$. Prove that
(a) $|LH| = |KM|$;
(b) the line through $B$ perpendicular to $DE$ bisects segment $HK$.

negatives.text:
Two circles $C_1$ and $C_2$, with centres at $D$ and $E$ respectively, touch at $B$. The circle with diameter $DE$ intersects $C_1$ at $H$ and $C_2$ at $K$, both on the same side of the line $DE$. Extending $HK$ meets $C_1$ again at $L$ and $C_2$ again at $M$. Prove that
