positive_text:
How many pairs of sequences $\left(d_{1}, d_{2}, \ldots, d_{2018}\right)$ and $\left(e_{1}, e_{2}, \ldots, e_{2018}\right)$ can be generated from a sequence $\left(x_{0}, x_{1}, \ldots, x_{2018}\right)$ of nonnegative integers satisfying the following:
- $0 \leq x_{i} < 2^{2018}$ for each $i$;
- $d_{i} = x_{i-1} + x_{i}$ and $e_{i} = x_{i-1} \mid x_{i}$ for each $1 \leq i \leq 2018$;
where $\mid$ is the bitwise or operation?

Let $\mathbb{Z}[x]$ be the ring of integer-coefficient polynomials in one variable. Determine all functions $\phi : \mathbb{Z}[x] \to \mathbb{Z}$ such that for all $f, g \in \mathbb{Z}[x]$,\begin{itemize}
    \item $\phi(f + 1) = \phi(f) + 1$, and
    \item if $\phi(f) \neq 0$ then $\phi(f)$ divides $\phi(f \cdot g)$.
\end{itemize}

negatives.text:
